To force a text field to display columns in Adobe, you can use the `RichText` class and its `setMultiline` method. However, this will not create a traditional multi-column layout. For a more complex layout, you can use the `RichText` class with a `TextFlow` object and a `ColumnLayout` object.

Here's an example code snippet that demonstrates how to create a text field with multiple columns:

```javascript
// Create a new text field
var textfield = new RichText();

// Create a new text flow
var textFlow = new TextFlow();

// Create a new column layout
var columnLayout = new ColumnLayout();

// Set the column layout to the text flow
textFlow.columnLayout = columnLayout;

// Set the text flow to the text field
textfield.textFlow = textFlow;

// Set the number of columns
columnLayout.numColumns = 3;

// Set the gutter between columns
columnLayout.gutter = 10;

// Set the column width
columnLayout.columnWidth = 100;

// Add the text field to the stage
stage.addChild(textfield);

// Set the text field's width and height
textfield.width = 400;
textfield.height = 200;

